# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# drive/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with pcb/ and cad/):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# - <filename>: exactly as it appears on disk. A suite going missing
#   (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing unregistered is a
#   loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
# - assertions=N: the suite must report exactly N total assertions
#   (passed+failed), so `check(true); quit(0)` planted above the real
#   assertions FAILS instead of passing a bare floor. Re-pin honestly when a
#   suite legitimately grows or shrinks.
# - real-worker: refused here — the attribute is a claim about a live worker
#   and drive ships no scripts/probe-worker-methods.py to back it.

# The real broker + real drive backend weigh a minerva_drive_list reply past
# the host's 64 KiB control cap and assert the panel drew a row for every
# project the worker sent. Pinned for a host where the drive plugin is
# already installed and built: an install (or its cargo_build pipeline) adds
# its own setup assertions, and the suite skips its live sections outright
# when drive-plugin is not built or when DRIVE_FOLDER does not reach the
# subprocess.
# 14 assertions = 4 setup (channel declared, start, panel, bulk route) + 2
# the backend answered at all and is working in the scratch folder + 4 the
# weighed reply + 3 the drawn rows + 1 teardown.
test_bulk_reply_seam.gd assertions=14

# The per-plugin CONTRACT GUARD: six domain-defined cases (null/empty, small
# and large x happy/unhappy, and the large-with-errors reply) driven through
# the real broker and the real drive-plugin subprocess, with the wire bytes of
# every large case printed on the Results line. Shares only its assertion
# discipline with the other plugins' guards (scripts/contract_guard.gd); the
# six cases, and drive's definition of "large" (tracked-file count), are its
# own. Same scratch-folder contract as the suite above: no case runs unless
# the backend confirms it is working in this suite's own folder.
#
# CASE 5 IS EXPECTED TO FAIL against drive as it stands, and its two
# assertions are the report: a state file that is not valid JSON is read as an
# EMPTY state (src/main.rs load_state ends in `unwrap_or_default()`), answered
# as a Drive with no projects, and then OVERWRITTEN with that empty state —
# the tracked set is destroyed and the reply says all is well. The assertions
# state the contract, not the behaviour. Do not weaken them to make the suite
# green; fix load_state.
#
# 28 assertions = 6 mount (db, the installed definition's channels, backend
# start, the bulk route, a status round trip, the scratch-folder gate) + 2
# null/empty + 3 small-happy + 3 small-unhappy (refusal + code, the tracked
# count is untouched) + 6 large-happy (request under the cap, reply over it,
# not an oversize refusal, success, the row count, the drawn rows) + 2
# large-unhappy + 5 large-with-errors (not oversize, success, every row
# unhappy, the row shape is the happy one's, still over the cap) + 1 teardown.
#
# `real-worker` is refused for drive (no scripts/probe-worker-methods.py), and
# this suite prints no such field. Without the built binary it SKIPS and
# reports no assertions, which the runner fails; the pin describes a host that
# has built and installed the plugin.
test_contract_guard.gd assertions=28
